    <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example34RazorCode" Id="example34">
        <div>
            <b>Style</b> and <b>Class</b> land on the root element, which inline styles and a single class cover
            well. For anything deeper, <b>Styles</b> and <b>Classes</b> reach the individual parts - the browse
            button, the description, the file list, each file item, its name, size, percentage, progress bar, status
            message and every action button and icon - and their <b>Dragging</b> entry applies to the root element
            only while files are being dragged over the component, which is how the examples below restyle the drop
            state without touching the idle look.
        </div>

        <br /><br />

        <div>Component's Style & Class:</div>
        <br />
        <div>
            <BitFileUpload Label="Styled file upload" UploadUrl="@UploadUrl"
                           Style="box-shadow: dodgerblue 0 0 1rem; border-radius: 1rem; padding: 0.5rem;" />
            <br />
            <BitFileUpload Label="Classed file upload" UploadUrl="@UploadUrl" Class="custom-class" />
